Impedance, resonance, passivity and quality factor (@em-impedance: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC", #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA", #electromagnetism "../magnetostatics/Magnetic-force-orbits-and-energy-transfer.lingua#r_34G06XMD2AYC7EC9ADQQNQFA0R", #electrical-power-engineering "../../../engineering/electrical-power-engineering/networks/Active-reactive-apparent-and-distorted-waveform-power.lingua#r_7ME7DSWC0ZMS4V97BTQGC5C323") { r_7ATZTVDYNEVH4RS80RSV55W07Y
**Read:** [Electromagnetics and Applications — David H. Staelin](../sources/Electromagnetics-and-Applications-Staelin.lingua#r_45QC1TW6RXJBJE8Q5H98DZT5AC), resonance and impedance applications; [Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA), transmission-line and impedance preliminaries.

Impedance is a port relation Ṽ/Ĩ for a stated frequency, amplitude regime and reference plane. A positive real part corresponds to passive average absorption under the chosen passive-current direction. Reactive signs depend on the phasor convention. A negative imaginary part with exp(−iωt) is inductive, not automatically a sign of gain.

Derive series RLC impedance and ω₀ = 1/sqrt(LC), then distinguish zero reactance, maximal current, stored-energy exchange and a measured resonant peak in a more complicated lossy system. The quality factor relates stored energy to loss per cycle under a specified resonance model. It need not equal every linewidth ratio once multiple modes, loading or strong dispersion matter.

Fit a frequency sweep with complex data rather than magnitude alone. Include cables, calibration plane, uncertainty and parameter correlation. An excellent fit over a narrow band can hide an unphysical extrapolation. Check DC/high-frequency limits and passivity; identify when distributed field effects require transmission lines or full Maxwell analysis. This makes the transition from introductory circuits to later wave and material inverse problems explicit.

**Continue:** [Magnetic force, orbits and energy transfer](../magnetostatics/Magnetic-force-orbits-and-energy-transfer.lingua#r_34G06XMD2AYC7EC9ADQQNQFA0R).

